<title>USA: ADM shareholder proposal defeated.</title>
<headline>ADM shareholder proposal defeated.</headline>
<dateline>DECATUR, Ill. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A shareholder proposal requiring Archer Daniels Midland Co to have a majority of independent directors was defeated at the annual meeting here on Thursday.</p>
<p>The measure, which many large shareholders had said was a key issue for the company, received 42 percent of votes cast, based on preliminary results, the company said.  </p>
<p>Other shareholder proposals covering director liability, confidential voting, board diversity and cumulative voting were also defeated.</p>
<p>The confidential voting measure received 46 percent of the vote.</p>
<p>	     Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
